    "productVersion": "1.0.0-beta.2",
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-05 14:41:58",
    "releaseNotes": "# AID v1.0.0-beta.2\n\n## 中文说明\n\n这是 AID 的第二个公开 Beta 测试版本。本次同版本强制重发同步更新服务端、后台管理端、Web 用户端、开源初始化 SQL 与升级器，重点完善源码构建式部署、供应链校验、配置管理和在线升级的可靠性。\n\n### 本次更新\n\n- 一键部署与升级继续采用三端同名 Tag 源码构建，不下载主程序大包；版本清单、三端源码与升级器均优先使用 Gitee，Gitee 不可用时整组切换到 GitHub，避免三个仓库混用不同来源。\n- 新增依赖区域策略 `auto / cn / global`。npm、Go、JDK、Node 与 Maven 下载均支持主源失败后切换备用源；线上 Maven 构建固定优先使用阿里云公共仓库，失败后使用原始 Maven Central 重新构建。\n- 三端源码构建会实时打印服务端、后台管理端、Web 用户端的依赖安装和编译日志；命令行部署同步归档到 `/data/aid/logs/`，后台一键升级同步写入升级器日志。\n- 修复 Web 用户端 `package-lock.json` 缺少 npm 10 所需可选 peer 记录的问题；发布机与服务器构建均强制读取各端 `packageManager` 的精确 npm 版本执行 `npm ci`，锁文件不一致时直接阻止发布，不再受宿主机 npm 版本漂移影响。\n- 固定构建工具链为 JDK 17.0.20、Node.js 22.22.0、Maven 3.9.9 和 Go 1.22.12，并对下载内容执行官方校验值验证，减少不同服务器环境导致的构建差异。\n- 所有安装环节统一遵循“存在且版本符合就跳过”。Docker Engine 24+ 与 Compose 2.20+ 缺失或过旧时先明确提示影响并询问管理员，只有确认后才从测速后的国内/官方 HTTPS 软件源安装；现有 `daemon.json` 永不被覆盖。\n- 手动 systemd 部署现在可按需准备 Git、JDK 17、Node.js、Maven、Go、Nginx、本机 MySQL 5.7.44 与 Redis 7.2.15。固定工具链和数据库归档必须通过官方摘要或 GPG 校验；外部 MySQL/Redis 只验证认证、连通性和版本，不修改外部服务。\n- RocketMQ 默认关闭且手动部署永不自动安装。Docker 可明确选择内置 MQ 或外部 MQ，配置组合不一致会在启动前阻止；外部 NameServer 至少一个节点可达才允许继续，内置 NameServer/Broker 必须通过健康检查。修改 MQ、Redis 或数据库配置后执行重启即可加载，不会重复初始化或重新安装已满足要求的组件。\n- RocketMQ 配置错误现在会打印实际配置文件路径，并给出关闭、Docker 内置、宿主机实例和其他服务器实例四种准确写法。Docker 外部 MQ 禁止使用指向业务容器自身的 `127.0.0.1`/`localhost`；宿主机实例使用 `host.docker.internal`。外部 NameServer 改为从临时 AID 容器网络实际探测，同时提示 Broker 的 `brokerIP1` 必须对容器可达。\n- Docker 官方基础镜像使用不可变摘要；国内镜像拉取后核对官方摘要，校验不一致时拒绝继续，防止标签漂移或镜像内容被替换。\n- Docker Hub 国内代理改为可配置的多候选列表：先探测 Registry 延迟，再验证当前镜像 manifest 并排序，最后按真实拉取结果逐源回退；后台部署配置可维护候选地址，已有配置升级只补缺项、不覆盖原值。\n- 升级时同步刷新受版本控制的部署脚本与 Docker Compose 文件，同时保留用户的 `.env` 和运行配置；Compose 只应用实际发生变化的服务配置，MySQL/Redis/RocketMQ 数据目录不会重新初始化。\n- Docker 与 systemd 部署继续坚持“先配置、确认后部署”。配置文件升级采用同目录备份和缺项补齐，既有配置值不覆盖；应用后自动重启并执行健康检查。\n- 首次初始化不再使用固定后台访问码。安装器会生成 12 位强随机访问码，已有非空访问码保持不变；后台管理端也只使用安全随机源生成访问码。\n- 外部或内置 MySQL、Redis、RocketMQ、HTTPS 证书与端口配置继续统一由部署配置管理；外部服务启用后不启动对应内置服务。\n- 修复分镜图片、视频生成链路中的任务续接、结果回填和错误归一化处理，并补充自动化回归测试。\n- Web 端完善视频预览交互与分集时间轴映射，新增时间轴映射测试；后台管理端补充依赖区域配置和访问码安全校验。\n- 更新 `sql/aid-init.sql` 与 `sql/v1.0.0-beta.2.sql`，用于全新安装和已有 Beta 环境的幂等升级。\n- Gitee Release 作为主下载源、GitHub Release 作为备用下载源，两端均只交付 Linux amd64/arm64 两个小型升级器，不上传主程序包、官方资产包或 `checksums.txt`。\n\n### 测试版提示\n\n本版本仍为 Beta 测试版。生产环境升级前请备份数据库、配置文件、上传目录和对象存储数据，并尽量在没有生成任务运行时执行升级。部署完成后请妥善保存安装器输出的后台访问路径，并立即修改默认管理员密码。\n\n## English Notes\n\nThis is the second public beta release of AID. This replacement release synchronizes the server, administration console, Web client, open-source SQL, and updater, with a focus on reproducible source builds, supply-chain verification, configuration safety, and reliable online upgrades.\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Installation and upgrades continue to build matching tags from all three repositories instead of downloading a large application archive. Manifests, source tags, and updater packages use Gitee first and switch all repositories to GitHub together only when Gitee is unavailable.\n- Added the `auto / cn / global` dependency-region policy. npm, Go, JDK, Node.js, and Maven downloads can retry through an alternate source. Server-side Maven builds always prefer the Aliyun public repository and retry the full build through the original Maven Central when needed.\n- Source builds now stream dependency and compilation logs for the server, administration console, and Web client. CLI deployments also archive the output under `/data/aid/logs/`, while one-click upgrades write the same output to the updater log.\n- Fixed the Web client's missing npm 10 optional-peer entry in `package-lock.json`. Both the publishing host and server-side source builder now execute `npm ci` with the exact npm version declared by each project's `packageManager`, blocking inconsistent lockfiles and eliminating host npm-version drift.\n- Pinned the build toolchain to JDK 17.0.20, Node.js 22.22.0, Maven 3.9.9, and Go 1.22.12, with official checksum verification for downloaded toolchains.\n- Every installation step now follows the same rule: skip an existing component only when its version satisfies the requirement. Missing or outdated Docker Engine 24+/Compose 2.20+ triggers an explicit risk notice and administrator confirmation before installation from speed-ranked domestic/official HTTPS repositories; an existing `daemon.json` is never overwritten.\n- Manual systemd deployment can now prepare Git, JDK 17, Node.js, Maven, Go, Nginx, a local MySQL 5.7.44 service, and Redis 7.2.15 as needed. Pinned toolchains and database archives require official checksums or GPG verification. External MySQL and Redis are only checked for authentication, reachability, and version and are never modified.\n- RocketMQ remains disabled by default and is never auto-installed for manual deployment. Docker can explicitly use either embedded or external RocketMQ; inconsistent settings are rejected before startup, external NameServers require at least one reachable node, and embedded NameServer/Broker services must pass health checks. Restarting after MQ, Redis, or database configuration changes reloads the configuration without reinstalling or reinitializing compliant components.\n- RocketMQ configuration errors now print the effective configuration-file path and actionable examples for disabled, embedded Docker, Docker-host, and remote-server setups. External RocketMQ in Docker rejects `127.0.0.1`/`localhost`, which points back to the application container; a host instance uses `host.docker.internal`. External NameServers are probed from a temporary AID container network, with an explicit reminder that the Broker `brokerIP1` must also be container-reachable.\n- Official Docker base images are pinned by immutable digest. Images fetched through the domestic mirror must match the official digest before they are accepted.\n- Docker Hub proxies now support a configurable candidate list. Registry latency and image-specific manifest availability determine the initial order, while actual pulls continue through every fallback; the list is manageable from deployment settings and upgrades only append a missing key without overwriting existing values.\n- Upgrades now refresh version-controlled deployment scripts and Docker Compose assets while preserving the user's `.env` and runtime configuration. Compose applies only services whose effective configuration changed, and MySQL/Redis/RocketMQ data directories are never reinitialized.\n- Docker and systemd deployments remain configuration-first. Configuration upgrades create a same-directory backup and add only missing keys without overwriting existing values, followed by restart and health verification.\n- Fresh installations no longer use a fixed administration access code. The installer generates a cryptographically strong 12-character code, while existing non-empty codes remain unchanged.\n- External and embedded MySQL, Redis, RocketMQ, HTTPS certificate, and port settings remain centrally managed. Embedded services are not started when external services are configured.\n- Improved storyboard image/video task continuation, result write-back, and normalized error handling, with additional regression tests.\n- Improved Web video-preview behavior and episode timeline mapping, and added administration controls for dependency regions and secure access-code validation.\n- Refreshed `sql/aid-init.sql` and `sql/v1.0.0-beta.2.sql` for clean installations and idempotent upgrades from existing beta deployments.\n- Gitee Release is the primary download source and GitHub Release is the fallback. Both contain only the small Linux amd64/arm64 updater archives; no application archive, official asset bundle, or `checksums.txt` is published.\n\n### Beta Notice\n\nThis remains a beta release. Back up the database, configuration files, upload directory, and object-storage data before upgrading a production environment, and avoid upgrading while generation tasks are active. Keep the generated administration URL secure and change the default administrator password immediately after deployment.",
